    '|a||Add the ratchet, the trap Soviet planners knew well: beat this year''s target by a lot, and next year''s goes up. So the smart worker holds back.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 9200
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy #ctx:1fz57f0'
    '|a||So pay pulls effort towards whatever is counted, and away from whatever is not.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 6160
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy #ctx:4xl1xh'
    '|a||Want the reason in symbols? Show the math, or skip it?':
      mp3: 
      ms: 3760
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy #ctx:1rehwum'
    '|a||Pay her a wage w, plus b per unit of the counted task and c per unit of the other, with eight hours to share.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 9400
      voice: gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy
    '|a||If b is bigger than c, every hour moved to the counted task pays more, so the hours keep drifting there.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 7280
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy #ctx:h0i136'
    '|a||So the two rewards have to match.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 2560
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy #ctx:c3565y'
    '|a||And if the second task can''t be measured, c is zero, so b must be zero too: a flat wage.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 6960
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy #ctx:1iusd47'
    '|a||So pay pulls effort towards what is counted. Then is a bonus always a mistake?':
      mp3: 
      ms: 6880
      voice: gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy
    '|b||Not at Safelite Glass, an American firm that fits car windshields. In 1994 and 1995 it switched its fitters from an hourly wage to pay per windshield.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 11080
      voice: 'gemini:Kore | sharp, friendly co-host: asks what a smart listener would, pushes back with real objections, sometimes explains; dry wit, never exaggerated; brisk lively pace, never slow #ctx:jdahc0'
    '|a||The economist Edward Lazear studied the records of about three thousand fitters. Call output per worker on the hourly wage a hundred. Guess what it became. Hourly wage = 100. Drag the bar to output per worker on pay per windshield.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 17520
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy #ctx:czxsj4'
    '|b||A hundred and forty-four. Forty-four percent more per worker, and the firm''s profits rose too.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 6480
      voice: 'gemini:Kore | sharp, friendly co-host: asks what a smart listener would, pushes back with real objections, sometimes explains; dry wit, never exaggerated; brisk lively pace, never slow'
    '|a||Part of it came from the same people working harder, part from who joined and who stayed: faster fitters liked the new pay.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 7240
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy #ctx:1lo25q5'
    '|b||And why no backfire? Because care was counted too. A windshield that broke came back to its fitter, to refit on his own time, paying for the glass.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 10640
      voice: 'gemini:Kore | sharp, friendly co-host: asks what a smart listener would, pushes back with real objections, sometimes explains; dry wit, never exaggerated; brisk lively pace, never slow #ctx:1kyvlbx'
    '|a||Lazear''s own caution: here output is easy to count, and the blame for a bad job is easy to assign. Managers'' and professionals'' jobs are rarely like that.':
